IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hrq-dates`
IMPORT `hrq-core`

-- Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) -- the questions of an individual affected by a Queensland public entity.
--
-- SEAT: the individual (for example a prisoner or someone held by police, a patient in a public hospital, a child in
-- State care, a person hurt by a council, a State agency or a contractor doing the State's work) who wants to know
-- whether the Act helps: "Do I have human rights under the Act?", "Is the body a public entity?", "Which of my rights
-- did what happened limit?", "Was the act unlawful?", "Can I add a human rights ground to my claim, and get damages?",
-- "Must the court read the statute in my case compatibly with my rights?", "Must I notify the Attorney-General and the
-- commission?", "Can I complain to the commissioner, and by when?", "What happens to my complaint?".
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list, a list of public holidays); each calls a rule
-- in hrq-core.l4. Judgments the Act leaves to a court or the commissioner are asked as "whether a court would find" or
-- "whether the commissioner considers" inputs, never decided. No question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT; the ss 52, 78
-- and 100 duties are built and run inside.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Rights Act 2019: the individual's questions`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 9-11 -- do I have rights, and is the body bound`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Do I have human rights under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 11? All individuals in Queensland have human rights; only individuals have them, so a company or other body has none.
GIVEN `individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an individual (a human being), not a company, association or other body
      `in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in Queensland when the act or decision affected you
GIVETH A `Who has human rights`
`Do I have human rights under the Act` `individual` `in Queensland` MEANS
    `s 11 -- has human rights` `individual` `in Queensland`

@export Is the body or person that acted or decided about me a "public entity" bound by the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 9-10? Departments, public servants, the police, councils, Ministers, statutory bodies and private bodies performing public functions for the State (such as a private prison operator or a funded housing provider) are; Parliament and courts, except when acting administratively, are not.
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body or person it was: a government entity (department or public service office); a public service employee; the Queensland Police Service or a police officer; a local government, councillor or council employee; a Minister; an entity established under an Act (a hospital and health service, statutory authority, public university); a member of a portfolio committee; a staff member or executive officer of a public entity; a registered NDIS provider; a non-State police officer; the Legislative Assembly; a court or tribunal; or another body or person not set up under an Act (a private company, care provider or contractor)
      `function` IS A `Kind of function` @desc What it was doing: operating a prison or other place of detention; emergency services; public health services; public disability services; public education; public transport; a housing service as a funded provider or the State; or another function
      `public nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For "another function" only: whether a court would find the function of a public nature (factors: conferred by statute, connected with government, regulatory, publicly funded, a government owned corporation; none conclusive). Answer no if not needed
      `for the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private body: whether it was performing the function for the State or a public entity (under contract or otherwise)
      `administrative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court, tribunal, the Legislative Assembly or a portfolio committee: whether it was acting in an administrative capacity rather than deciding a case or conducting proceedings
      `works for a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a staff member or executive officer: whether the body they work for is a public entity
      `non-State officer acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a non-State police officer: whether they were appointed a special constable, authorised to exercise a police officer's powers, or exercising a power under another Queensland law
      `prescribed to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation prescribes the body to be a public entity (not deposited; answer no if you do not know)
      `prescribed not to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation prescribes the body not to be a public entity (not deposited; answer no if you do not know)
      `s 60 declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body has asked the Minister to declare it subject to the obligations of a public entity, and the declaration is in force (s 60)
GIVETH A `Public entity`
`Is the body a public entity` `kind` `function` `public nature` `for the State` `administrative` `works for a public entity` `non-State officer acting` `prescribed to be` `prescribed not to be` `s 60 declaration` MEANS
    `s 9 -- public entity` `kind` `function` `public nature` `for the State` `administrative` `works for a public entity` `non-State officer acting` `prescribed to be` `prescribed not to be` `s 60 declaration`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 2 -- which of my rights did what happened limit`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Did what happened to me limit my right to life under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 16? Every person has the right to life and the right not to be arbitrarily deprived of life. Lists each limb your facts meet; an empty list means none on these facts.
GIVEN `life limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the act or failure limited your right to life (for example by exposing you, while held or in care, to a real risk to your life that the entity knew or ought to have known of)
      `a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a life was taken (for a claim about a death)
      `arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a life was taken, whether a court would find the deprivation of life arbitrary
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Did what happened limit my right to life` `life limited` `a death` `arbitrary` MEANS
    `s 16 -- limbs limited` `life limited` `a death` `arbitrary`

@export Did what happened to me limit my protection from torture and cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 17? You must not be tortured, treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way, or subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without your full, free and informed consent. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `tortured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were subjected to torture
      `cruel or degrading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way
      `medical treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment (for example sedation or restraint while held)
      `consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you gave your full, free and informed consent to it
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Did what happened limit my protection from cruel treatment` `tortured` `cruel or degrading` `medical treatment` `consented` MEANS
    `s 17 -- limbs limited` `tortured` `cruel or degrading` `medical treatment` `consented`

@export Did what happened to me limit my right to privacy and reputation under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 25? You have the right not to have your privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with, and not to have your reputation unlawfully attacked. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `interfered with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your privacy, family, home or correspondence was interfered with (for example a search, surveillance, disclosure of health records, removal of a child)
      `unlawful interference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the interference unlawful
      `arbitrary interference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the interference arbitrary (unreasonable or disproportionate, even if lawful)
      `reputation attacked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your reputation was attacked
      `unlawful attack` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the attack on your reputation unlawful
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Did what happened limit my right to privacy` `interfered with` `unlawful interference` `arbitrary interference` `reputation attacked` `unlawful attack` MEANS
    `s 25 -- limbs limited` `interfered with` `unlawful interference` `arbitrary interference` `reputation attacked` `unlawful attack`

@export Did what happened to me as a child limit my right to protection under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 26(2)? Every child has the right, without discrimination, to the protection needed by the child, and in the child's best interests, because of being a child (for example a child in State care harmed by abuse or neglect).
GIVEN `a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) when it happened
      `protection lacking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were not given the protection you needed, and that was in your best interests, because of being a child
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Did what happened limit my protection as a child` `a child` `protection lacking` MEANS
    `s 26(2) -- limbs limited` `a child` `protection lacking`

@export Did my arrest or detention limit my right to liberty and security under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 29? Covers arbitrary arrest or detention, detention without lawful grounds and procedures, not being told the reason, delay in being brought before a court or to trial, automatic detention awaiting trial, the court's handling of an application about the lawfulness of detention, and imprisonment for a contractual debt. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `liberty limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find your right to liberty and security was limited in some other way
      `arrested or detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were arrested or detained
      `arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the arrest or detention arbitrary
      `lawful grounds and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were deprived of liberty on grounds, and by procedures, established by law
      `told the reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were told the reason for the arrest or detention at the time
      `proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proceedings were to be brought against you
      `promptly told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were promptly told about them
      `criminal charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were arrested or detained on a criminal charge
      `promptly before a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were promptly brought before a court
      `trial without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were brought to trial without unreasonable delay (answer yes if the trial has not yet been unreasonably delayed)
      `released` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were released
      `automatic detention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while awaiting trial, you were automatically detained in custody (rather than detention being decided case by case)
      `applied to court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to a court for a declaration or order about the lawfulness of your detention
      `decided without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court decided without delay
      `found unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the court found the detention unlawful
      `ordered release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it did, whether the court ordered your release
      `contract debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were imprisoned only because you could not perform a contractual obligation (such as paying a debt)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Did my arrest or detention limit my right to liberty` `liberty limited` `arrested or detained` `arbitrary` `lawful grounds and procedures` `told the reason` `proceedings` `promptly told` `criminal charge` `promptly before a court` `trial without delay` `released` `automatic detention` `applied to court` `decided without delay` `found unlawful` `ordered release` `contract debt` MEANS
    `s 29 -- limbs limited` `liberty limited` `arrested or detained` `arbitrary` `lawful grounds and procedures` `told the reason` `proceedings` `promptly told` `criminal charge` `promptly before a court` `trial without delay` `released` `automatic detention` `applied to court` `decided without delay` `found unlawful` `ordered release` `contract debt`

@export Was my right to humane treatment while deprived of liberty limited under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 30? Everyone deprived of liberty must be treated with humanity and respect for their dignity; a person detained but not convicted must be kept apart from convicted persons unless reasonably necessary, and treated as appropriate for someone not convicted. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `deprived of liberty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were deprived of liberty (in prison, a watch-house, youth detention, or held in a hospital or care facility)
      `humane treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find you were treated with humanity and with respect for your inherent dignity
      `unconvicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were detained as an accused person or without charge (not convicted)
      `with convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were held with persons convicted of offences
      `reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find that was reasonably necessary
      `treated as unconvicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If unconvicted, whether you were treated in a way appropriate for a person not convicted
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Was my right to humane treatment limited` `deprived of liberty` `humane treatment` `unconvicted` `with convicted` `reasonably necessary` `treated as unconvicted` MEANS
    `s 30 -- limbs limited` `deprived of liberty` `humane treatment` `unconvicted` `with convicted` `reasonably necessary` `treated as unconvicted`

@export Was my right to a fair hearing limited under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 31? A person charged with an offence or a party to a civil proceeding has the right to have it decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing (the public may be excluded in the public interest or the interests of justice), and judgments must be publicly available. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `charged or a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were charged with a criminal offence or are a party to a civil proceeding
      `competent and impartial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court or tribunal was competent, independent and impartial
      `fair hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the hearing fair
      `public hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hearing was public
      `exclusion justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was not public, whether the exclusion was in the public interest or the interests of justice
      `judgment available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment or decision is publicly available
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Was my right to a fair hearing limited` `charged or a party` `competent and impartial` `fair hearing` `public hearing` `exclusion justified` `judgment available` MEANS
    `s 31 -- limbs limited` `charged or a party` `competent and impartial` `fair hearing` `public hearing` `exclusion justified` `judgment available`

@export Were my rights as a child in the criminal process limited under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 33? An accused or uncharged child who is detained must be kept apart from all detained adults (no exception); an accused child must be brought to trial as quickly as possible; a convicted child must be treated as appropriate for their age. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a child (under 18) at the time
      `accused or uncharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an accused child, or a child detained without charge
      `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been convicted of an offence
      `detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were detained
      `with adults` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you were held with detained adults
      `trial quickly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If accused, whether you were brought to trial as quickly as possible
      `treated for age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If convicted, whether you were treated in a way appropriate for your age
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Were my rights as a child in the criminal process limited` `a child` `accused or uncharged` `convicted` `detained` `with adults` `trial quickly` `treated for age` MEANS
    `s 33 -- limbs limited` `a child` `accused or uncharged` `convicted` `detained` `with adults` `trial quickly` `treated for age`

@export Was my right to health services limited under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 37? Every person has the right to access health services without discrimination, and must not be refused emergency medical treatment immediately necessary to save their life or prevent serious impairment. Lists each limb your facts meet.
GIVEN `access limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your access to health services was refused or limited
      `discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether that was discrimination on the basis of an attribute in the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (for example age, impairment, race, sex)
      `emergency refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were refused emergency medical treatment
      `immediately necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the treatment was immediately necessary to save your life or prevent serious impairment
GIVETH A LIST OF `Right limb`
`Was my right to health services limited` `access limited` `discrimination` `emergency refused` `immediately necessary` MEANS
    `s 37 -- limbs limited` `access limited` `discrimination` `emergency refused` `immediately necessary`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 8, 58 -- was the act or decision unlawful`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Was the act or decision compatible with my human rights under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 8? It is compatible if it limits no human right, or limits one only to the extent reasonable and demonstrably justifiable in a free and democratic society (s 13).
GIVEN `right limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the act or decision limited one of your human rights (any right in ss 15-37)
      `justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the limit reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13 (weighing the right, the purpose, whether the limit helps achieve it, less restrictive ways, and the balance)
GIVETH A `Compatibility`
`Was the act compatible with my human rights` `right limited` `justified` MEANS
    `s 8 -- compatible with human rights` `right limited` `justified`

@export Was the act or decision of the public entity unlawful under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 58? It is unlawful for a public entity to act or decide incompatibly with human rights, or, in deciding, to fail to give proper consideration to a relevant human right; unless it could not reasonably have acted differently because of a law, it is a religious body acting by its doctrine, or the act was of a private nature. A failure to act counts as an act. An unlawful act is not invalid for that reason, and is not an offence (s 58(6)).
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What kind of body or person it was (see the public entity question)
      `function` IS A `Kind of function` @desc What it was doing (see the public entity question)
      `public nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For "another function": whether a court would find it of a public nature
      `for the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a private body: whether it was performing the function for the State or a public entity
      `administrative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court, tribunal, the Legislative Assembly or a portfolio committee: whether it was acting in an administrative capacity
      `works for a public entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a staff member or executive officer: whether the body they work for is a public entity
      `non-State officer acting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a non-State police officer: whether appointed, authorised or exercising a Queensland power
      `prescribed to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation prescribes the body to be a public entity (answer no if you do not know)
      `prescribed not to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation prescribes the body not to be a public entity (answer no if you do not know)
      `s 60 declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a declaration under s 60 is in force for the body
      `before commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or decision was before the Human Rights Act commenced (the day fixed by proclamation, not in the Act)
      `private nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the act or decision of a private nature (for example a purely commercial or employment matter rather than a public function)
      `religious body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body was established for a religious purpose and acted in accordance with its religion's doctrine, as necessary to avoid offending its people's religious sensitivities
      `no choice under law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the entity could not reasonably have acted or decided differently because of a statutory provision, a Commonwealth or other State law, or otherwise under law
      `right limited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find the act or decision limited one of your human rights
      `justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the limit reasonable and demonstrably justifiable under s 13
      `a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a decision (rather than only an act or failure to act)
      `right relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a decision, whether a human right was relevant to it
      `proper consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether a court would find the entity gave proper consideration to that right (at least identifying the rights affected and considering whether the decision would be compatible)
GIVETH A `Unlawful under s 58`
`Was the act unlawful under the Act` `kind` `function` `public nature` `for the State` `administrative` `works for a public entity` `non-State officer acting` `prescribed to be` `prescribed not to be` `s 60 declaration` `before commencement` `private nature` `religious body` `no choice under law` `right limited` `justified` `a decision` `right relevant` `proper consideration` MEANS
    `s 58 -- unlawful`
        (`is a public entity` (`s 9 -- public entity` `kind` `function` `public nature` `for the State` `administrative` `works for a public entity` `non-State officer acting` `prescribed to be` `prescribed not to be` `s 60 declaration`))
        `before commencement` `private nature` `religious body` `no choice under law`
        (`s 8 -- compatible with human rights` `right limited` `justified`)
        `a decision` `right relevant` `proper consideration`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 59 -- what the Act adds to my claim`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Can I add a human rights ground to my claim against a public entity under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 59? The Act gives no claim of its own. If, apart from the Act, you can seek relief or a remedy about the act or decision on the ground that it was unlawful (for example judicial review, or a claim for false imprisonment or battery), you may seek the same relief on the ground that it was unlawful under s 58, even if your other ground fails.
GIVEN `other ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, apart from the Human Rights Act, you can seek relief or a remedy about the act or decision on the ground that it was unlawful (judicial review, a claim in tort, a statutory claim), as that other law gives
      `unlawful under s 58` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act or decision was unlawful under s 58 (the answer to the s 58 question)
GIVETH A `A human rights ground`
`Can I add a human rights ground to my claim` `other ground` `unlawful under s 58` MEANS
    `s 59 -- a human rights ground` `other ground` `unlawful under s 58`

@export Can I get damages because a public entity acted unlawfully under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland)? No: s 59(3) bars damages on the ground of unlawfulness under s 58. Any right to damages you have apart from the Act (for example in negligence) is not affected (s 59(6)).
GIVEN `damages otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a right to damages apart from the Human Rights Act (for example under a claim in negligence, for false imprisonment, or under a compensation statute)
GIVETH A `Damages`
`Can I get damages for the unlawfulness` `damages otherwise` MEANS
    `s 59(3), (6) -- damages` `damages otherwise`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 48, 49 -- reading the statutes in my case, and referral (only if my case is in a court or tribunal)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Must the statute that decides my case be read compatibly with my human rights under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 48? Every Queensland Act and statutory instrument must, so far as possible consistently with its purpose, be interpreted compatibly with human rights, or else most compatibly; but not a provision under an override declaration in force (s 45), and an incompatible provision stays valid.
GIVEN `kind of law` IS A `Kind of law` @desc The law in question: a Queensland Act; a Queensland statutory instrument (regulation, rule or other instrument made under a Queensland Act); a Commonwealth Act or instrument; the common law; or the law of another State, Territory or country
      `proceeding before commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your court proceeding was commenced (or concluded) before the Human Rights Act commenced
      `override made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Parliament has made an override declaration for the provision (an express declaration that it has effect despite being incompatible with human rights)
      `override commenced` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the provision containing the declaration (or its re-enactment) commenced, as an ISO date (any date otherwise)
      `earlier expiry stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the Act states an expiry day earlier than 5 years after commencement
      `earlier expiry` IS A DATE @desc If so, that earlier expiry day, as an ISO date (any date otherwise)
      `day of reading` IS A DATE @desc The day the court reads the provision (for example the day of the hearing), as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Reading compatibly`
`Must the statute be read compatibly with my rights` `kind of law` `proceeding before commencement` `override made` `override commenced` `earlier expiry stated` `earlier expiry` `day of reading` MEANS
    `s 48 -- reading compatibly` `kind of law` `proceeding before commencement` `override made` `override commenced` `earlier expiry stated` `earlier expiry` `day of reading`

@export Can the human rights question in my case be referred to the Supreme Court under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 49? Only if a question of law about the Act's application, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with it, arises; a party applies; and the court or tribunal considers it appropriate. A referral by the Trial Division goes to the Court of Appeal.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Court` @desc The court or tribunal: the Supreme Court (Trial Division); the District Court; the Land Court; the Land Appeal Court; or another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates Court or QCAT)
      `question arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question of law about the application of the Human Rights Act, or about interpreting a statutory provision in accordance with it, arises in your proceeding
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party (you or another) has applied for the question to be referred
      `appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court or tribunal considers the question appropriate to be decided by the Supreme Court
GIVETH A `Referral`
`Can my question be referred to the Supreme Court` `court` `question arises` `applied` `appropriate` MEANS
    `s 49 -- referral` `court` `question arises` `applied` `appropriate`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 52 -- notifying the Attorney-General and the commission (only if I raise the Act in court)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Must I notify the Attorney-General and the Queensland Human Rights Commission because my case raises the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 52? A party must give notice in the approved form if a question about the Act's application, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with it, arises in the Supreme, District, Land or Land Appeal Court, or a question is referred to the Supreme Court under s 49; not to the Attorney-General if the State is a party, nor to the commission if it is a party.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the District Court; the Land Court; the Land Appeal Court; or another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates Court or QCAT)
      `question arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question of law about the application of the Act, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with it, arises in your proceeding
      `referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question has been referred to the Supreme Court under s 49
      `State a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State of Queensland is a party to the proceeding
      `commission a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Queensland Human Rights Commission is a party to the proceeding
GIVETH A `Notices I must give`
`Must I notify the Attorney-General and the commission` `court` `question arises` `referred` `State a party` `commission a party` MEANS
    `s 52 -- notices I must give` `court` `question arises` `referred` `State a party` `commission a party`

@export Have I given the notices the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 52 requires of me as a party? Notice in the approved form to the Attorney-General (unless the State is a party) and to the commission (unless it is a party). The Act sets no time for it; court rules may.
GIVEN `court` IS A `Court` @desc The court: the Supreme Court; the District Court; the Land Court; the Land Appeal Court; or another court or tribunal
      `question arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question of law about the application of the Act, or about interpreting a statute in accordance with it, arises in your proceeding
      `referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a question has been referred to the Supreme Court under s 49
      `State a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the State of Queensland is a party to the proceeding
      `commission a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Queensland Human Rights Commission is a party to the proceeding
      `AG notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Attorney-General notice in the approved form
      `commission notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the commission notice in the approved form
GIVETH A `Notices given`
`Have I given the notices` `court` `question arises` `referred` `State a party` `commission a party` `AG notified` `commission notified` MEANS
    `s 52 -- have I given the notices` `court` `question arises` `referred` `State a party` `commission a party` `AG notified` `commission notified`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 63-70 -- complaining to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export Who may make a human rights complaint to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 63-64? The individual the public entity's alleged contravention of s 58(1) was about, their agent, or a person the commissioner authorises in writing because the individual can not complain.
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am` @desc Who you are: the individual the alleged contravention was about; their agent; a person the commissioner has authorised in writing; or someone else
      `public entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is about a public entity's act or decision (see the public entity question)
      `individual can not complain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an authorised person: whether the commissioner is satisfied the individual can not make the complaint
GIVETH A `May I complain`
`Who may complain to the commissioner` `who I am` `public entity` `individual can not complain` MEANS
    `ss 63, 64 -- may I complain` `who I am` `public entity` `individual can not complain`

@export From what day can I complain to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner, after first complaining to the public entity, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 65(1)(b)? At least 45 business days must have passed since your complaint to the public entity. Gives the first day after the 45th business day.
GIVEN `day complained to entity` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your complaint to the public entity, as an ISO date
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The Queensland public holidays (where you are) on weekdays after that day, as ISO dates; give none if none
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can I complain to the commissioner` `day complained to entity` `public holidays` MEANS
    `s 65(1)(b) -- the earliest day` `day complained to entity` `public holidays`

@export Can I make my human rights complaint to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner now, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 65? Only if you first complained to the public entity, at least 45 business days have passed, and you have had no response or one you consider inadequate; the commissioner may accept it earlier because of exceptional circumstances.
GIVEN `complained to entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have complained to the public entity about the alleged contravention (for example under its complaints procedure), so that the commissioner can be satisfied you did
      `day complained to entity` IS A DATE @desc The day you complained to the public entity, as an ISO date
      `day of my complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) your complaint to the commissioner, as an ISO date
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The Queensland public holidays on weekdays between those days, as ISO dates; give none if none
      `had a response` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the public entity has responded to your complaint
      `response inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you consider the response inadequate
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner considers it appropriate, because of exceptional circumstances, to accept your complaint before the 45 business days pass
GIVETH A `Can I complain now`
`Can I complain to the commissioner now` `complained to entity` `day complained to entity` `day of my complaint` `public holidays` `had a response` `response inadequate` `exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `s 65 -- can I complain now` `complained to entity` `day complained to entity` `day of my complaint` `public holidays` `had a response` `response inadequate` `exceptional circumstances`

@export By when should I make my human rights complaint to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner so it is within 1 year after the alleged contravention, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 70(1)(d)? A complaint made later may be refused (it is not barred outright). Gives the last day: the anniversary of the contravention.
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the public entity's alleged contravention (the act, failure to act or decision) happened, as an ISO date
GIVETH A DATE
`By when should I complain to the commissioner` `day of contravention` MEANS
    `s 70(1)(d) -- the last day` `day of contravention`

@export Can the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner refuse my complaint as too late under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 70(1)(d)? The commissioner may refuse a complaint not made within 1 year after the alleged contravention; if refused, it lapses and you can not complain again about it.
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the alleged contravention happened, as an ISO date
      `day of my complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) your complaint to the commissioner, as an ISO date
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`Can my complaint be refused as late` `day of contravention` `day of my complaint` MEANS
    `s 70(1)(d) -- in time` `day of contravention` `day of my complaint`

@export Can I both wait the 45 business days after complaining to the public entity and still complain to the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner within 1 year of the contravention, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 65 and 70(1)(d)?
GIVEN `day of contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the alleged contravention happened, as an ISO date
      `day complained to entity` IS A DATE @desc The day you complained (or will complain) to the public entity, as an ISO date
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The Queensland public holidays on weekdays after that day, as ISO dates; give none if none
GIVETH A `Both periods`
`Can I meet both time periods` `day of contravention` `day complained to entity` `public holidays` MEANS
    `ss 65, 70 -- can I meet both periods` `day of contravention` `day complained to entity` `public holidays`

@export Is my human rights complaint in the form the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 67 and 102 require? It must be written, state your name and an address for service (residential, business, post office box or email), and give enough detail of the alleged contravention; the commissioner must help you put it in writing if you need help.
GIVEN `written` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is in writing
      `name stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states your name
      `address` IS A `Kind of address` @desc The address for service it gives: a residential address; a business address; a post office box address; an email address; or none (or another kind)
      `enough details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes enough detail to show the alleged contravention (what the public entity did or decided, and which right)
GIVETH A `Form of complaint`
`Is my complaint in the required form` `written` `name stated` `address` `enough details` MEANS
    `ss 67, 102 -- form of complaint` `written` `name stated` `address` `enough details`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 69-89 -- what happens to my complaint (once it is made)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

@export What happens if the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner refuses to deal with my complaint, or defers it, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 71-72? A refused complaint lapses and you can not complain again about the same contravention, unless it was refused because the s 65 steps were not met; a deferral does not end it. You must be given notice and reasons.
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What the commissioner did` @desc What the commissioner did: refused as frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance; refused for a more appropriate course under another law; refused as already dealt with by another entity; refused as the s 65 steps were not met; refused as out of time; refused to continue for non-compliance with a reasonable request, non-cooperation or no contact; or deferred it
GIVETH A `After refusal`
`What happens if my complaint is refused` `what happened` MEANS
    `ss 71, 72 -- after refusal` `what happened`

@export Can my human rights complaint be passed to another body (the ombudsman, the health ombudsman, the Crime and Corruption Commission, the information commissioner, the NDIS commissioner, or the Anti-Discrimination Act process), or from one of them to the human rights commissioner, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 66, 73 and 75? Only with your consent.
GIVEN `where to` IS A `Where to` @desc Which passing-on: to the ombudsman, health ombudsman, Crime and Corruption Commission, information commissioner or NDIS commissioner; to be dealt with under the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991; or from one of those bodies to the human rights commissioner
      `consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consent
      `more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner considers it would be more appropriately dealt with there (not needed for a referral to the human rights commissioner)
GIVETH A `Passing on`
`Can my complaint be passed to another body` `where to` `consent` `more appropriate` MEANS
    `ss 66, 73, 75 -- passing on` `where to` `consent` `more appropriate`

@export What must the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner give me at each stage of my human rights complaint under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 71, 73, 76, 88 and 89?
GIVEN `stage` IS A `Stage` @desc The stage: refused; deferred; referred to another entity; accepted for resolution; finished and not resolved; or resolved
GIVETH A `What I must be given`
`What must the commissioner give me` `stage` MEANS
    `what the commissioner must give me` `stage`

@export Must I give the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner information about my complaint when asked, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 78? You must comply with a direction (not a mere request) within the period stated unless you have a reasonable excuse, such as legal professional privilege; a direction can be filed with a court and enforced as a court order.
GIVEN `direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice directs you to give the information (rather than only asks)
      `purpose stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the purpose of the request
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable excuse (for example the information is subject to legal professional privilege)
GIVETH A `Information duty`
`Must I give the commissioner the information` `direction` `purpose stated` `reasonable excuse` MEANS
    `s 78 -- must I give the information` `direction` `purpose stated` `reasonable excuse`

@export Have I complied in time with the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner's direction to give information under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 78(5)?
GIVEN `direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice directs you to give the information (rather than only asks)
      `purpose stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the purpose of the request
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable excuse (for example legal professional privilege)
      `day of notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the notice, as an ISO date
      `last day stated` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period stated in the notice, as an ISO date
      `gave it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the information
      `day gave it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you gave it, as an ISO date (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A `Complied in time`
`Have I complied with the direction in time` `direction` `purpose stated` `reasonable excuse` `day of notice` `last day stated` `gave it` `day gave it` MEANS
    `s 78 -- complied in time` (`s 78 -- must I give the information` `direction` `purpose stated` `reasonable excuse`) `day of notice` `last day stated` `gave it` `day gave it`

@export Must I attend the conciliation conference on my human rights complaint in person, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 82? Yes, unless you are a child or a person with impaired capacity, or the commissioner consents to someone attending for you; you may bring a support person with consent, and an interpreter.
GIVEN `child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a child (under 18)
      `impaired capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have impaired capacity (within the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000)
      `consent for another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has consented to another person attending the conference for you
GIVETH A `Attend in person`
`Must I attend the conciliation conference in person` `child` `impaired capacity` `consent for another` MEANS
    `s 82 -- must I attend in person` `child` `impaired capacity` `consent for another`

@export Can I be represented by a lawyer or another person at the conciliation conference, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 83? Only with the commissioner's consent.
GIVEN `consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has consented to your being represented
GIVETH A `Representation`
`Can I be represented at the conciliation conference` `consented` MEANS
    `s 83 -- may I be represented` `consented`

@export Can what was said at the conciliation conference, or the commissioner's report on my unresolved complaint, be used in court, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) ss 86 and 88(6)? Not unless you and the respondent agree.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want to use` @desc What you want to use: something said or done in the conciliation conference; or the commissioner's report on your unresolved complaint
      `proceeding` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc The proceeding: one about a contravention of the Human Rights Act; or another civil, criminal or administrative proceeding (for example your claim in negligence)
      `both agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both you and the respondent agree
GIVETH A `Admissible`
`Can the conference or report be used in court` `what` `proceeding` `both agree` MEANS
    `ss 86, 88(6) -- admissible` `what` `proceeding` `both agree`

@export Can the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner publish information about my complaint, including my personal information, under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 90? The power is for a complaint the commission has finished dealing with, and never extends to your personal information unless you published it or gave it for publication first.
GIVEN `finished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commission has finished dealing with your complaint
      `I published it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously published the personal information, or given it for the purpose of publication
GIVETH A `Publication`
`Can the commissioner publish my information` `finished` `I published it` MEANS
    `s 90 -- publication` `finished` `I published it`

@export Am I protected from liability for giving information about a human rights complaint under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 99? If you act honestly in giving information under the Act to the commissioner or another entity about a complaint, you are not liable civilly, criminally or administratively for it, and are not taken to breach professional ethics.
GIVEN `honest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted honestly in giving the information
      `about a complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave it under the Act, to the commissioner or another entity, about a human rights complaint
GIVETH A `Protected`
`Am I protected for giving information` `honest` `about a complaint` MEANS
    `s 99 -- protected` `honest` `about a complaint`

@export Have I breached an anonymity direction of the Queensland Human Rights Commissioner under the Human Rights Act 2019 (Queensland) s 100? If the commissioner directs that information identifying a person involved in a complaint not be disclosed, you must comply unless you have a reasonable excuse; the maximum penalty for an individual is 35 penalty units.
GIVEN `direction covers it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a commissioner's direction under s 100 prohibits disclosing the information (information that identifies, or is likely to identify, a person involved in the complaint)
      `reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable excuse for disclosing it
      `disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you disclosed the information
GIVETH A `Anonymity`
`Have I breached an anonymity direction` `direction covers it` `reasonable excuse` `disclosed` MEANS
    `s 100 -- anonymity` `direction covers it` `reasonable excuse` `disclosed`
